quran[5]{c,v,t}:
  2,220,"upon this world and the Hereafter. They ask you about orphans. Say: ‘(Making an effort for) improving their condition is best. So, if you intermingle with them (by becoming their partners), they are your brothers. Allah knows the one who is corrupt from the one who reforms. Had Allah willed, He would have put you in hardship. Indeed, Allah is All-Mighty, All-Wise.’"
  2,221,"Do not marry idolatrous women unless they believe. A believing slave girl is better than an idolatress, although she may please you. Do not wed (your daughters with) idolaters unless they believe. A believing slave is better than an idolater, although he may please you. They invite (others) to the Fire, but Allah invites (them) to Paradise and forgiveness by His Will. He clarifies His revelations for the people so that they may be mindful of advice."
  2,222,"They ask you about (intercourse during) menstruation. Say: ‘It is hurtful.’ So, keep away from (your) wives during (their) menstrual periods, and do not approach them until they are (again) clean. And when they become clean, you may approach them as Allah has commanded you. Indeed, Allah loves those who strive for repentance. And He loves those who strive to purify themselves."
  2,223,Your wives are (like) your fields; go to your fields whenever you like. And send ahead (good deeds) for your souls and be God-conscious. Bear in mind that you shall meet Him. Give glad tidings to the believers.
  2,224,"(O believers!) Do not make (the name of) Allah a hindrance through your oaths from being pious and God-conscious and from making peace between people. Allah is All-Hearing, All-Knowing."
